      "speaker": "narrator",
      "t0": 0.08,
      "t1": 3.58,
      "text": "An enemy radar crew sees a giant bomber outside, yet their screen shows nothing."
    },
    {
      "id": "L2",
      "beat": "B2_FACETS",
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "t0": 3.75,
      "t1": 8.88,
      "text": "Normal jets reflect radar straight back for a missile lock, but this B-2 uses angled facets to bounce waves sideways."
    },
    {
      "id": "L3",
      "beat": "B3_SDUCTS",
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "t0": 9.08,
      "t1": 15.82,
      "text": "Even its spinning metal turbines stay hidden, buried deep inside curved S-shaped tunnels that trap radar pulses until they die."
    },
    {
      "id": "L4",
      "beat": "B4_RAM_BEE",
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "t0": 16.02,
      "t1": 21.82,
      "text": "Then its carbon skin swallows leftover waves as tiny heat, shrinking an eighty-ton jet into a bumblebee."
    },
    {
      "id": "L5",
      "beat": "B5_BLUEPRINT",
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "t0": 22.02,
      "t1": 25.88,
      "text": "Inside the cockpit, the pilot glides past missile radar, deflecting every pulse away."
    },
    {
      "id": "L6",
      "beat": "B6_FINAL",
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "t0": 26.08,
      "t1": 29.85,
      "text": "By the time enemies spot that tiny speck, the bomber is already overhead."
    }
  ],
